        "text": "The target is an Idaho state row, not a national total or weighted average. Dataset 5abea2e0-3f8e-4b49-a50d-d63d5fd9103c distinguishes original O and updated U submissions. The ledger does not explicitly identify the denominator; I use CMS's published ex parte-rate definition: beneficiaries renewed ex parte divided by beneficiaries due for renewal. The [June state table](https://www.medicaid.gov/resources-for-states/downloads/eligib-oper-and-enrol-snap-jun2026.pdf) explicitly labels this denominator. Resolution remains the first official O print, rounded to one decimal."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Historical anchors come from the current reporting-month original outcomes in CMS's first-release snapshot tables, excluding quarterly updated outcomes. CMS publishes these historical percentages rounded to whole percentage points. Attempts to fetch the raw Idaho O rows through the dataset API and CSV failed; precise historical numerator counts and one-decimal ratios were not fetched. The historicalContext values preserve the available official rounded prints."
      },
      {
        "kind": "tool",
