        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The outside-view reference class is twelve consecutive Idaho original-month prints from July 2025 through June 2026. Its base rate has mean 57.5%, median 52.5%, and range 45%-95%. The February spike reversed immediately; autumn also showed substantial variation. I therefore favor persistence with a modest prior-August anchor over extrapolating the latest monthly increase."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Release-date verification limitation: the [official CMS publication page](https://www.medicaid.gov/medicaid-and-chip-eligibility-operations-and-enrollment-snapshot) lists June 2026 as released September 25, 2026, and May 2026 as released August 28, 2026. No fetched official calendar or announcement confirms December 15, 2026 for August data. I retain the supplied ledger resolutionDate, but cannot satisfy the requirement to independently verify that date; it is not inferred from historical cadence."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use an equal-weight blend of June persistence and the prior-August print. Level is 51%; the seasonal anchor adds 1.5 percentage points. Additional momentum, one-off, and policy-mechanism adjustments are each zero; February's spike remains in interval dispersion. The twelve-print sample yields eleven successive changes [0,13,1,-2,-20,3,46,-46,-4,1,5], with mean -0.2727 and squared deviations summing to 4856.1818. Thus sigma = 22.0367 percentage points = sqrt(4856.1818/10). The nominal Gaussian 80% half-width is 1.28*sigma = 28.2070 points. Scaling by sqrt(2) for two unobserved monthly transitions gives 39.8908 points, implying final rounded bounds 12.6%-92.4%."
      },
